# The webui is served by an aggregating Caddy that is SAME-ORIGIN with the
# agent RPC: `/` serves the static build, `/agent.v1.*` is reverse-proxied to
# the agent over h2c. This is why the browser needs only a token — the API base
# is always this page's own origin.
#
# AGENT_UPSTREAM IS REQUIRED. There is no default, on purpose — and the requirement is enforced by
# `tool/entrypoint.sh`, NOT by this file.
#
# `{$AGENT_UPSTREAM}` expands to an EMPTY string when the variable is unset, and Caddy accepts that:
# it starts, serves /srv, and answers 502 on every /agent.v1.* request. So a Caddyfile with no
# default does not fail — it fails SILENTLY, which is how the old default behaved too.
#
# There used to be a default: a cluster name from whichever environment built the image. A
# deployment that did not set the variable came up HEALTHY, because static assets are local, and
# breakage appeared only at login, with the cause visible only in Caddy's log:
#     dial tcp: lookup standalone-agent.temp.svc.cluster.local: no such host
#
# The entrypoint now refuses to start without it, so the failure lands at deploy time. Set it to the
# in-cluster agent, e.g. `agent.dev.svc.cluster.local:80`.
:8080 {
	handle /healthz {
		respond "ok" 200
	}

	# Connect RPC (AgentService / AdminService) -> agent over cleartext HTTP/2.
	handle /agent.v1.* {
		reverse_proxy {$AGENT_UPSTREAM} {
			transport http {
				versions h2c
			}
		}
	}

	# Static SPA with client-side routing fallback.
	handle {
		root * /srv
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}

	log {
		output stdout
		format console
	}
}
